task: frame-rebind (after a restart, a frame read back from a journal is re-bound to rebuilt descriptors by an explicit request that reports what it re-derived)
agent: okay-42
started: 2026-09-07
branch: feature/frame-rebind

why: BACKLOG frame-rebind: `valueOf` matches a slot by identity, so a
  frame read back with rebuilt `Slot` values cannot be read unless the
  caller threads the new descriptors through everything (TestWalk hit
  it; the rule is documented). `Frame.rebind(slots)` makes the restart
  case ordinary -- and the hazard is why it is explicit and reports:
  re-deriving a value re-parses the stored text, and "next Tuesday"
  against a new reference day is a different date. So: rebind by name,
  re-parse each stored text with the new descriptor, and answer the
  frame together with what changed (name, before, after) and what could
  no longer be read; the caller decides. Laws in okay-frame; a temporal
  case in okay-intent shows the date moving and being reported.
